  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 119.0,
  "event_seq": 294,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul) to 1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-04). The evidence best supports a billing-import validation defect as the dominant mechanism: rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01, compares raw AMI register values to 12-month m3 history with no unit scaling (E-13), while firmware v4.2 meters (rollout 2026-06) report register values in 0.1 m3 units rather than m3 (E-14); this causes legitimate reads to be misread as high-consumption and rejected at billing import, exactly matching the pattern in 1184/1240 (95.5%) disputed ESTIMATED-read bills, which show an AMI read received before cutoff but rejected as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION (E-12). Rejected reads trigger estimate substitution, producing the disputed bill."
 },
