  "root_problem": "Billing dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul) to 1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-04). Current evidence confirms that billing-import rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 to compare raw AMI register values against 12-month m3 history with no unit scaling (E-13), combined with firmware v4.2 meters (rollout 2026-06) reporting register values in 0.1 m3 units instead of m3 (E-14), causes legitimate high-consumption rejections (REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION) that reproduce in 1184 of 1240 (95.5%) disputed ESTIMATED-read bills (E-12, E-15). E-16 confirms this defect is confined to the ESTIMATED-read minority (1240/3025, 41%): the 1184 affected accounts it identified are all ESTIMATED read type with zero ACTUAL, so a separate, as-yet-unidentified billing-import mechanism must account for the 1785 ACTUAL-read disputed bills (59%, the majority of the surge)."
